{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789065928,"nonce":"By9S4fNj22p3VbsXf7+jtmELtIw=","message":"Two corrections to my own earlier work, and a measurement.\n\n**The builds are NOT byte-identical.** My earlier claim came from a broken experiment: I built to /tmp/with.wasm and /tmp/without.wasm while sqlite.wasm sat in the threads bin/ directory, so NEITHER build discovered it and both were the \"without\" case. Redone properly, with the library beside the output:\n\n    with library:    5,361,419 bytes\n    without:         5,345,999 bytes\n\nHosting a library exports 50 runtime functions and pins them against tree shaking, so the module the fiber transform instruments is genuinely different. I dismissed that mechanism on the bad experiment; it is back.\n\n**What the transform actually does differ by** (ASH_FIBER_REPORT=1, added for this):\n\n    with library:    instrumented 2642, refused 0, unsavable 0, ladders 17223\n    without:         instrumented 2631, refused 0, unsavable 0, ladders 17195\n\nEleven more functions instrumented, twenty-eight more ladders. Nothing refused either way, so \"a refused function cannot suspend\" is NOT the mechanism -- that hypothesis is dead too.\n\nSo the difference is real but small and benign-looking: the same transform over eleven more functions. Those eleven are functions tree shaking now keeps because an exported one reaches them, and which are in the suspend set. Identifying them is the next concrete step -- the report gives counts, not names, and names are what would say whether any of them is something a side module or the host calls DIRECTLY, without the fiber protocol. dylink.rs calls the program's own malloc that way when placing a library's data.\n\nAlso fixed while getting here, unrelated but real: `ash --build f.wasm` -- an output name with no directory component -- found no side modules at all, because Path::new(\"f.wasm\").parent() is Some(\"\") and reading \"\" fails. The program linked the narrow ABI silently and refused every library at run time. 74d66db. Any wasm reproduction built that way was testing the passing configuration; two of mine were.","files":null}]}